  "prompt": "You are an expert JavaScript developer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a fully playable \"Tango\" logic puzzle game.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. No external libraries.\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nTHEME & VISUALS:\n1. The game must look polished and modern, utilizing a clean, balanced interface.\n2. The grid must be 6x6 cells.\n3. The two playing symbols MUST be the Fire emoji (\ud83d\udd25) and the Ice Cube emoji (\ud83e\uddca).\n4. Constraint markers must clearly sit on the borders between adjacent cells using an Equals sign (=) or a Cross (\u00d7).\n\nCORE GAMEPLAY RULES:\n1. Row and Column Balance: Every row and every column must contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca.\n2. No Three in a Row: You cannot place three identical symbols adjacent to each other horizontally or vertically.\n3. Constraint Markers:\n   - '=' (Equals): The two adjacent cells must contain the same symbol.\n   - '\u00d7' (Cross): The two adjacent cells must contain opposite symbols.\n4. Interactivity: Clicking a cell should cycle its state: Empty -> \ud83d\udd25 -> \ud83e\uddca -> Empty.\n\nBACK-END LOGIC & PROCEDURAL GENERATION SPECS:\nThe game MUST generate a brand new, random, playable board on every page load. Implement the generation using this sequence:\n1. Solution Generation (Backtracking): Write a recursive backtracking function to generate a fully populated, valid 6x6 grid that obeys the Balance and No-Three-In-A-Row rules. \n2. Constraint Placement: Once a valid solved board exists, randomly select 6 to 8 pairs of adjacent cells. If the cells share the same symbol, place an '=' marker between them. If they are different, place an '\u00d7' marker.\n3. Puzzle Creation: After placing constraints, randomly clear (empty) 70% of the cells, leaving a few starting symbols and the constraint markers as hints for the player.\n4. Validation: Implement a \"Check Solution\" button that compares the user's current grid against the underlying rules (Balance, No-Three-In-A-Row, and Constraints). Highlight any errors in red.\n\nEnsure the state management clearly separates the \"solution board\" from the \"player board\", and that markers overlay the grid lines cleanly using CSS absolute positioning or a highly refined Grid layout.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Tango Puzzle</title>\n<style>\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    background: #fafafa;\n    color: #333;\n  }\n  #grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 80px);\n    gap: 2px;\n    height: 100vh;\n    margin: 20px auto;\n  }\n  .cell {\n    width: 80px;\n    height: 80px;\n    background: #f0f0f0;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    font-size: 1.5rem;\n    cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  .cell:hover {\n    background: #e0e0e0;\n  }\n  .constraint {\n    position: absolute;\n    width: 1.2em;\n    height: 1.2em;\n    pointer-events: none;\n    text-anchor: middle;\n  }\n  #checkBtn {\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n    font-size: 1rem;\n    cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  #validationErrors {\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    white-space: pre;\n    background: #fff4dd;\n    padding: 0.5rem;\n    border-left: 4px solid #d4a017;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"grid\"></div>\n<div id=\"constraints\"></div>\n<button id=\"checkBtn\">Check Solution</button>\n\n<script>\nconst ROWS = 6;\nconst COLS = 6;\nconst SYM1 = '\ud83d\udd25';\nconst SYM2 = '\ud83e\uddca';\nconst EMPTY = -1;\nlet solution = null;\n\nfunction solve() {\n  const board = Array.from({ length: ROWS }, () => Array(COLS).fill(EMPTY));\n  const rowCounts = Array.from({ length: ROWS }, () => [0, 0]); // 1 = \ud83d\udd25, 2 = \ud83e\uddca\n  const colCounts = Array.from({ length: ROWS }, () => [0, 0]);\n\n  function hasThreeInRow(r, c, sym) {\n    if (c < 2) return false;\n    let cnt = 0;\n    for (let i = c - 2; i <= c; i++) {\n      const v = board[r][i];\n      if (v === sym) cnt++;\n      else cnt = 0;\n      if (cnt >= 3) return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  function backtrack(r, c) {\n    if (c === COLS) {\n      solution = [row.slice() for row in board];\n      return true;\n    }\n    const nextCol = c + 1;\n    if (nextCol >= COLS && backtrack(r, nextCol)) return true;\n    if (board[r][c] !== EMPTY) {\n      if (nextCol >= COLS) return backtrack(r, nextCol);\n    }\n    // try \ud83d\udd25\n    if (rowCounts[r][1] < 3 && colCounts[c][1] < 3 && !hasThreeInRow(r, c, SYM1)) {\n      board[r][c] = 1;\n      rowCounts[r][1]++;\n      colCounts[c][1]++;\n      if (backtrack(r, nextCol)) return true;\n      board[r][c] = EMPTY;\n      rowCounts[r][1]--;\n      colCounts[c][1]--;\n    }\n    // try \ud83e\uddca\n    if (rowCounts[r][2] < 3 && colCounts[c][2] < 3 && !hasThreeInRow(r, c, SYM2)) {\n      board[r][c] = 2;\n      rowCounts[r][2]++;\n      colCounts[c][2]++;\n      if (backtrack(r, nextCol)) return true;\n      board[r][c] = EMPTY;\n      rowCounts[r][2]--;\n      colCounts[c][2]--;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (backtrack(0, 0)) return true;\n  return false;\n}\n\nfunction generateMarkers() {\n  const pairs = [];\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      if (c + 1 < COLS) pairs.push([r, c, 'R']);\n      if (r + 1 < ROWS) pairs.push([r, c, 'D']);\n    }\n  }\n  const chosen = new Set();\n  const min = Math.ceil(0.3 * ROWS * COLS);\n  const max = Math.floor(0.8 * ROWS * COLS);\n  let count = Math.random() * (max - min + 1) + min;\n  while (chosen.size < count) {\n    const idx = Math.floor(Math.random() * pairs.length);\n    chosen.add(pairs[idx]);\n  }\n  return Array.from(chosen);\n}\n\nfunction clearCells(player) {\n  const total = ROWS * COLS;\n  const toClear = Math.ceil(0.3 * total);\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      if (player[r][c] !== EMPTY) continue;\n      if (Math.random() < 0.7) {\n        player[r][c] = EMPTY;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderBoard(player, solution) {\n  const container = document.getElementById('grid');\n  container.innerHTML = '';\n  const cellWidth = 80;\n  const rowHeight = 100;\n  const containerSize = document.documentElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const grid = document.createElement('div');\n  grid.style.width = `${containerSize.width}px`;\n  grid.style.height = `${containerSize.height}px`;\n  grid.style.position = 'relative';\n  container.appendChild(grid);\n  const constraints = document.getElementById('constraints');\n  constraints.innerHTML = '';\n  for (const [r, c, dir] of markerPairs) {\n    const left = dir === 'R' ? `${r},${c + 0.5}` : `${r + 0.5},${c}`;\n    const top = dir === 'D' ? `${r + 0.5},${c}` : `${r},${c + 0.5}`;\n    const el = document.createElement('span');\n    el.className = 'constraint';\n    el.textContent = dir;\n    el.style.left = left;\n    el.style.top = top;\n    constraints.appendChild(el);\n  }\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      const cell = document.createElement('div');\n      cell.className = 'cell';\n      if (player[r][c] === SYM1) cell.textContent = SYM1;\n      else if (player[r][c] === SYM2) cell.textContent = SYM2;\n      constraints.appendChild(cell);\n      if (player[r][c] !== EMPTY) {\n        cell.style.background = player[r][c] === SYM1 ? SYM1 : SYM2;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateBoard() {\n  const errors = [];\n  // row balance\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    let cnt1 = 0, cnt2 = 0;\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      const v = solution[r][c];\n      if (v === 1) cnt1++;\n      else if (v === 2) cnt2++;\n    }\n    if (cnt1 !== 3 || cnt2 !== 3) errors.push(`Row ${r+1} does not contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca`);\n  }\n  // column balance\n  for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n    let cnt1 = 0, cnt2 = 0;\n    for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n      const v = solution[r][c];\n      if (v === 1) cnt1++;\n      else if (v === 2) cnt2++;\n    }\n    if (cnt1 !== 3 || cnt2 !== 3) errors.push(`Column ${c+1} does not contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca`);\n  }\n  // no three in a row\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      if (solution[r][c] === 1) continue;\n      if (solution[r][c+1] === 1 && solution[r][c+2] === 1) errors.push(`Row ${r+1}, cols ${c+1}-${c+3} have three consecutive \ud83d\udd25`);\n      if (solution[r][c] === 2 && solution[r][c+1] === 2 && solution[r][c+2] === 2) errors.push(`Row ${r+1}, cols ${c+1}-${c+3} have three consecutive \ud83e\uddca`);\n      if (solution[r+1][c] === 1 && solution[r+1][c+1] === 1 && solution[r+1][c+2] === 1) errors.push(`Column ${c+1}, rows ${r+1}-${r+3} have three consecutive \ud83d\udd25`);\n      if (solution[r+1][c] === 2 && solution[r+1][c+1] === 2 && solution[r+1][c+2] === 2) errors.push(`Column ${c+1}, rows ${r+1}-${r+3} have three consecutive \ud83e\uddca`);\n    }\n  }\n  // constraint markers\n  const dirs = { 'R': '=', 'D': '\u00d7' };\n  const placed = new Set(markerPairs);\n  for (const p of markerPairs) {\n    const [r, c, dir] = p;\n    const left = dir === 'R' ? `${r},${c + 0.5}` : `${r + 0.5},${c}`;\n    const top = dir === 'D' ? `${r + 0.5},${c}` : `${r,${c + 0.5}`;\n    const el = document.createElement('span');\n    el.className = 'constraint';\n    el.textContent = dir;\n    el.style.left = left;\n    el.style.top = top;\n    document.getElementById('constraints').appendChild(el);\n  }\n  if (errors.length) {\n    document.getElementById('checkBtn').style.color = 'red';\n    const errDiv = document.createElement('div');\n    errDiv.id = 'validationErrors';\n    errDiv.textContent = `<strong>Errors:</strong> ${errors.join('<br>') || 'No errors'}`;\n    document.body.appendChild(errDiv);\n  } else {\n    document.getElementById('checkBtn').style.color = 'black';\n  }\n}\n\nlet markerPairs = [];\n\nfunction init() {\n  // generate solution\n  solution = null;\n  if (!solve()) {\n    console.warn('Could not generate solution');\n    return;\n  }\n  // generate markers\n  markerPairs = generateMarkers();\n  // clear 70% of cells\n  clearCells(solution);\n  const total = ROWS * COLS;\n  const toClear = Math.ceil(0.3 * total);\n  for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      if (Math.random() < 0.7) {\n        solution[r][c] = EMPTY;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  renderBoard(solution, null);\n}\n\nsetTimeout(init, 2000);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
